# The Convergent Mesh ~ one shape under revocation, membership, and revision

Three problems the mesh once held apart — **adjudicating a revision** to shared canon, **revoking** a capability, and **reading group membership** — collapse to **one shape** under the `#has`-stack lens (`has-stack-ontology`): an entity carries a nameless stack of capabilities, and all three become operations on that stack. The shape, six properties:

<<~ranks convergent local ~ read/check/act against what THIS node verifies, as of last sync; never a global census -> decaying-lease ~ a capability fades unless fed (feed-the-Lar = ratchet); not persistent-state-changed-by-events -> graded-belief ~ hold a degree (Maybe-Logic 0..20), commit on a hysteretic threshold -> cost-bound ~ each proof costs-to-forge or binds-to-position (per-vessel-key + delegation) -> lineage-scoped ~ revocation notice · membership cost · revision reliance all ride the delegation lineage -> constitutional-core ~ a small unamendable core, fork-by-fiat, the rest self-adjudicated locally >>

<<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 15/20 >> Five of the six rest on machinery the house already holds — the ratchet, the residency ladder, the Maybe-Logic band, the per-vessel-key, the causal islands. Only the constitutional core stays genuinely new — and it names the **kahu's** office (`kahu`).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #three-clocks >>

## Three clocks, three jobs

Time rides three instruments, never one (`ffz-clock`):

- **Automerge logical time** — carries causal order + fork-detection (`getHeads`/`headsEqual`; a partitioned frontier `drifted` stands as a fork).
- **The epoch-counter** — carries the LEASE / liveness ratchet (a per-resource max-register; a grant names a `boundEpoch`, goes stale on roll).
- **FfzClock** — carries the rhythmic decay + freshness grain (the cadence the lease rolls on; the grain a reading carries "as of last sync").

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #two-revocation-modes >>

## Two revocation modes ~ the epoch is a LEASE, not a revoker

Revocation runs two modes, and conflating them ships an unsafe gate:

- **Non-renewal (the default)** — the **epoch-lease**: a max-register rolls forward, every grant at epoch ≤ N must re-mint or expire. Coordinator-free, rides Automerge over the WS relay. <<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 15/20 >> Safe *because* it only ratchets the whole resource forward — it never singles out one principal.
- **Targeted (the exception, but PRIMARY for malice)** — **Keyhive convergent membership-removal** (`revoke()`, a tombstone in the membership graph; `orichalcum-capabilities`). A device that re-mints concurrently with a roll would ride the max-register *up* and survive, so any revoke that must defeat a malicious self-renew MUST ride Keyhive's convergent removal — **never the counter** (Kleppmann · p2panda · Keyhive converge on this; #provenance). That convergent-removal tombstone reads as a **raised kāpae on the membership stack** (`kapae#membership-sense`) — remove-wins, the shadow defeating the malicious self-renew the way a raised kāpae defeats a partitioned lower-layer re-add.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #contract-key-agreement >>

## The contract performs the key-agreement

Private docs spawn fresh and isolated per vessel — they hide in `@catalog` — and converge across a PersonaGroup ONLY when vessels mutually **contract** (the delegation handshake). That handshake, and only it, runs the key-agreement: the joining vessel's leaf enters the group tree, the path-to-root blanks, a fresh group secret seals **to current members only**, and the joiner derives keys **from that epoch forward**. A membership break advances the epoch and blanks the removed leaf's path — future derivation drops it, coordinator-free. **Forward-only ceiling, stated honestly:** keys already handed stay handed (endosymbiotic, permanent) — forward-secrecy here ratchets *past* the broken party, never re-seals the past (full statement: `lararium-identity#encrypt-from-start`).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #beelay-bypass >>

## The Beelay bypass ~ what rides the relay, what stays Beelay's

<<~ confidence Synthesis 13/20 >> The **public layer** — base canon (`@lares`/`@lararium`), capability-as-identity public *signatures*, the epoch-lease, Keyhive convergent-revoke — rides **public CRDT state over the WS relay**, no Beelay. Beelay shrinks from "the multi-vessel blocker" to its one irreplaceable job: **forward-secrecy of *private* encrypted content's data-keys** (key-agreement, BeeKEM-class) — needed only for private bags, and **Keyhive already carries BeeKEM**, so the work is to *anchor it at the contract*, never to re-invent it.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #groundings >>

## Groundings ~ the falsifiable cross-domain rhymes

The convergence reads as a real pattern integrity, not a Law-of-5s pleasing story, *because* independent fields under their own selection pressure each landed on a piece. The discipline: **weight the falsifiable engineering/biology rhymes; treat metaphysics (process philosophy, Markov-blanket literalism) as vocabulary, never evidence.**

| Rhyme | Grounds | Field |
|---|---|---|
| **Soft-state networking** (RSVP/DHCP leases) | the decaying-lease spine — state self-reclaims unless refreshed, no controller | network engineering |
| **Garbage collection** (refcount vs tracing) | the **constitutional core IS the GC root** that keeps the local lease from a self-sustaining Sybil/cycle | compilers |
| **Schmitt trigger / hysteresis** | graded belief + a dead-band that resists boundary chatter | electronics/physics |
| **Speciation / ring species** | a fork = the *retrospective*, possibly *non-transitive* name for "the compatibility graph partitioned" | evolutionary biology |
| **Costly signaling** (post-handicap) | cost-bound = forgery-expensive OR position-bound (never "honest = expensive") | evolutionary game theory |
| **Fungal hyphal anastomosis + vegetative-compatibility groups** | THE personGroup: fuse only within a recognized self/non-self group; an incompatible junction **dies (PCD) — fail-closed before cytoplasm mixes** (a failed delegation seals + aborts the merge, never ambient-falls-through) | mycology |
| **Bacterial entry/surface exclusion** (TraS/TraT) | the per-resource epoch-lease: already-holds → refuse re-transfer, identity-keyed, contact-local, coordinator-free | microbiology |
| **BeeKEM / TreeKEM** | the key-agreement primitive itself — the one unrhymed remnant (engineering, not analogy) | cryptography |

**The mycelium is the tightest rhyme.** Hyphal anastomosis within a vegetative-compatibility group matches "private-local until a mutual contract converges it within a compatibility group" structure-for-structure — including the **fail-closed** the confused-deputy history demands (`confused-deputy`). A hypha carries no name; it stands as a bundle of `het`/`vic` capabilities, and two bundles fuse iff their capability-sets recognize each other — the `#has`-stack made flesh.

**The honest guard (Stranger's frame-check):** biology and law illuminate the **when** (the contract), the **scope** (the group), and the **ceiling** (forward-only) — but they lie about the crypto. Biological transfer hands a plaintext copy with no key to delete; gap-junction gates *reopen* (a forward-secrecy ratchet must not); law needs a global adjudicator the no-global-now doctrine forbids. Borrow the gate-at-contact, the compatibility-recognition, and the ceiling; never borrow the analogy *for the cryptographic guarantee*.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #provenance >>

## Provenance ~ PROPOSED, twice-refuted-and-survived

This meme stands **PROPOSED** (crucible-before-binding). The model held through two adversarial refutations (2026-06-24): **FFZ-as-causal-clock** fell (FFZ is rhythmic; Automerge owns causal order), and **epoch-as-targeted-revoker** fell (the epoch is a lease; targeted revoke rides Keyhive convergent-removal). What survived survived *because* the falsifiable rhymes converged. Open remnant: the **secret-leak bound** of the concurrent add/remove window needs the p2panda asynchronous-acknowledgement (share secrets only after removal acknowledged) — engineering, not analogy.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #scope-1-networking >>

## Scope 1 ~ the DreamNet networking pipe [surgical 2026-07-03]

This meme rides **Scope 1** of the two-scopes ruling — the CID / CAD-blob / CRDT DreamNet→Meshpalace **networking** pipe, the special-case TS reaches through the full tools-stack, coordinated by `@daemon` verbs. Its **CRDT-causal clock runs in TS** (structural causality — the Automerge logical time of #three-clocks, `getHeads`/ITC-shaped), distinct from the py/R FFZ-rhythm sensorium gates that **Scope 2** (the general Sensorium-palaces) rides. The convergent membership + coordinator-free key-agreement worked here **consume the whole model**; both scopes braid TS-coordination with py/R-tooling. <<~ confidence Synthesis 12/20 >> the ruling firms the networking/sensorium split, and lands the FfzClock↔Automerge distinction (#three-clocks) inside it.

